    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d487">

                <pb facs="0519" n="507" sameAs="frus:frus1945v08/pg507"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.00/12–2045: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Iran</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Murray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-12-20T16:00:00+03:25">December 20,
                            1945—4 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 21—6:10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1165. Embtel 1062, Dec 4. Prime Minister today ordered steps taken for
                    establishment of local councils in provinces and towns throughout Iran except in
                    Azerbaijan. Unless there is Majlis objection, Govt contemplates early elections
                    to put this plan into effect.</p>
                <p>Embassy understands this is work of Interior Minister Saleh<anchor n="32"
                        xml:id="d487-f1"/> who was known to favor such councils and who apparently
                    lost no time in putting ideas into effect upon assuming Interior portfolio.</p>
                <p>Sent Dept 1165, repeated Moscow 363, London 144.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Murray</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d487-f1" n="32" xml:id="d487-f1-content">
                <p>The Ambassador reported in telegram 1160, December 20, 1945, 2 p.m., the
                    appointment of Mr. Saleh as Minister of Interior as part of a reshuffling of the
                    Hakimi Cabinet. His predecessor, Khalil Fahimi, was described in the telegram as
                    “anathema to Russians and pro-Russian elements here.” (891.002/12–2045)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
